== To the Reader

CHRISTIAN READER:

#smallcaps[There] are two things, which I have always looked upon as difficult: The one is, to make the #emph[Wicked sad;] they want not cause of sadness, they are #emph[taken captive by Satan] #footnote[#emph[2 Tim 2:25.]]: This is all that is gotten by fighting on the Devils side; he doth not make his Soldiers #emph[Captains,] but #emph[Captives,] he leads them Prisoners before him, and at last will give them damnable pay: Yet so are sinners #emph[blinded by the God of this world] #footnote[#emph[2 Cor 4:4.]], that they cannot see the chains they are held in, but kiss their fetters, and go laughing to Hell. The other puzling difficulty, is, to make the #emph[Godly joyful:] Though they have enough to rock their troubled hearts quiet, & may #emph[encourage themselvs in the Lord their God;] yet like the froward child, they put away the breast, and refuse to be comforted. #emph[Amnon,] though a Kings Son, was lean #footnote[#emph[2 Sam 13:4.]]. This dejection in the Godly, ariseth from a double Spring; either because their inward comforts are darkned, or their outward comforts are disturbed: To cure both which troubles, I have put forth this ensuing Piece, hoping by the blessing of God, it will buoy up their disponding hearts, and make them look with a more pleasant aspect; I would prescribe them to take now & then a little of this #emph[Cordial.] When the Prophet #emph[Eliah]'s spirits were ready to faint under the #emph[Juniper Tree,] the Angel set before him a #emph[Cake,] and a #emph[Cruse of Water,] & when he had eaten he was cheered, and went in the strength of that meat, till he came unto #emph[Horeb the Mount of God] #footnote[#emph[1 Kgs 19:8.]]. Me-thinks this Text, like that sweet repast, may very much corroborate and strengthen the Saints in their journey to Heaven, and may be as a sacred feather, to drop the golden Oyl of consolation into their hearts: #emph[All things shall work together for good, to them that love God.] To knew that nothing shall hurt the godly, is matter of comfort#footnote[#emph[Ps 91:10.]]\; but to be assured that all things which fall out, shall co-operate for their good, that their crosses shall be turned into blessings, the bloody showrs of affliction shall water the withering root of their Grace, and make it flourish more; here is that may fill their hearts with joy till they run over. It will be no small revivement to me, if these Labours of mine prove advantagious to any. When S. #emph[Pauls] Prison would not admit him the liberty of a Pulpit, he wrote some Epistles, the benefit whereof the Church of God hath reaped in after-ages. When I am at present taken off from my publick employment of preaching, I shall be glad if I may be useful by writing; and while I my self am in #emph[a civil sence] dead I may make others in #emph[a spiritual sence] alive: This is the Prayer of him, who is

#v(1em)

#align(right)[Thy Friend, in all true Affection & Devotion. THOMAS WATSON.]
